# Print command help for `z4x prepare` (`-z4x-cmd-prepare`).

eval "$_z4x_opt"

print -Pr -- "$(<<\END
%F{4}Usage:%f %F{2}z4x%f %Bprepare%b [-a|--all] [<plugin>]...

Prepare the specified core plugins by invoking their corresponding preparation
function %F{2}-z4x-prepare-<plugin>%f.

The special plugin name "self" prepares z4x itself by invoking
%F{2}-z4x-prepare-self%f which compiles all z4x source files and generates the
z4x-specific %F{2}compinit%f implementation.

If %B-a%b or %B--all%b is specified, all core plugins including "self" will be
prepared.

Examples:

  %F{2}z4x%f %Bprepare%b self

  %F{2}z4x%f %Bprepare%b powerlevel10k zsh-history-substring-search

  %F{2}z4x%f %Bprepare%b -a
END
)"

# vim:ft=zsh
